services.comment:
Teams: the unit of tenancy. A team is a console team, a Kubernetes
namespace and a catalog folder, all one name. Its lifecycle: created,
retired (reversible, read-only), purged (its name stays reserved).

methods.comment:
Whether the team's members must sign in with single sign-on: then no
password signs them in, and their password sessions end. Admins only;
admins themselves are exempt. Has no effect while single sign-on is off.

services.comment:
Bots and their API tokens. A team's bot acts as a member of that team;
an automation token belongs to no team and can do exactly what its scopes
say. A token is shown once, when it's made, and only its hash is kept.

fields.comment:
"kernel": kernel policy, from the catalog release it verified itself,
into policies this console may only read (beside this console's own);
"console": this console (the kernel's catalog policy isn't installed);
"unknown": it couldn't be read.

What the caller may see: every line for the step's team (and admins);
for anyone else who can see the run, only lines the step logged as
JSON with "level": "info" (a plain line counts as debug).

Whether an action's product is for this install (Product.runs_here);
for a template, whether every step's is. Run, a schedule or an order
of one that isn't is refused (NOT_FOR_THIS_INSTALL).
